cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroForge in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NeuroForge: A Local-First Neuroimaging Research Platform"
version: 0.1.0-alpha
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SadhanaArivoli/neuroforge"
abstract: >
  NeuroForge is a local-first neuroimaging research platform that connects
  datasets, pipelines, runs, artifacts, provenance records, and publication
  outputs in a unified workspace. It wraps established neuroimaging tools
  (FSL, FreeSurfer, fMRIPrep, MRIQC, Nilearn, and others) without
  reimplementing their algorithms, providing artifact-typed pipeline chaining,
  automatic methods generation, citation assembly, and reproducible study
  reports.
authors:
  - family-names: Arivoli
    given-names: Sadhana
    email: "arivolit@gmail.com"
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - fMRI
  - MRI
  - BIDS
  - reproducibility
  - provenance
  - functional connectivity
  - research software
date-released: "2026-07-13"
